ies are performed so everything goes well.\r\n\r\nI than added a new endpoint with some @RestForm attributes and I had this errror\r\n`java.lang.IllegalStateException: You have attempted to perform a blocking operation on a IO thread. This is not allowed, as blocking the IO thread will cause major performance issues with your application. If you want to perform blocking EntityManager operations make sure you are doing it from a worker thread.\r\n`\r\n\r\nwhich means that the @Blocking annotation is not working.\r\nI tried also to add the annotation directly on the method but the result was the same.\r\n\r\nThan I removed the form parameters and for testing purpose added them as path parameters and the query was performed.\r\n\r\nThis is my endpoint\r\n\r\n**IO THREAD ERROR**\r\n` @POST\r\n  @PermitAll\r\n  @Blocking\r\n  @Consumes(MULTIPART_FORM_DATA)\r\n  @Produces(APPLICATION_JSON)\r\n  public Uni<Response> generateToken(@RestForm String username, @RestForm String password) {\r\n    return this.userService.authenticate(username, password)\r\n        .map(response -> Response.ok().entity(response).build());\r\n  }`\r\n\r\n**NO ERRORS**\r\n`  @POST\r\n  @Path(\"/{username}/{password}\")\r\n  @PermitAll\r\n  @Blocking\r\n  @Consumes(TEXT_PLAIN)\r\n  @Produces(APPLICATION_JSON)\r\n  public Uni<Response> generateToken(String username, String password) {\r\n    return this.userService.authenticate(username, password)\r\n        .map(response -> Response.ok().entity(response).build());\r\n  }`\r\n\r\nCurrently I'm using v1.11.1\r\n\r\nAm I doing something wrong? \r\nThank you very much\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"stuartwdouglas","id":328571,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODU3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/328571?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartwdouglas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/